meta {
  name: 07 Remove student
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/centers/me/students/{{studentId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.removed: eq true
}

docs {
  Frees the seat immediately. Check `Center Subscription / 02 Get usage` before
  and after — `seatsUsed` drops by one, and the seat is usable again straight
  away.

  This UNLINKS rather than deletes. The account, the password the student chose,
  and every attempt they ever submitted survive; only the tie to this center is
  cut. Deleting would destroy a person work because an administrator tidied a
  roster.

  To confirm, look the row up directly in the database afterwards: it is still
  there, with `center_id` NULL and `password_hash` intact.

  Afterwards the student no longer appears in `01 List students`, and
  `03 Get student` answers 404 — the center genuinely cannot reach them any more.
}
